    "notes": "1. 'total_revenue' is composed of 'Product' and 'Service and other' line items, which sum to the reported 'Total revenue'.\n2. 'total_operating_cost' includes all costs and expenses deducted from revenue to arrive at 'Operating income'. This comprises 'Total cost of revenue' (split into 'Product' and 'Service and other') and the operating expenses: 'Research and development', 'Sales and marketing', and 'General and administrative'.\n3. 'net_income' is the final 'Net income' line.\n4. 'taxes' is the 'Provision for income taxes'.\n5. 'interest_expenses' is the 'Interest expense' component from the supplementary table for 'Other Income (Expense), Net'. The value is reported as a positive number as it is an expense that reduces income.\n6. All numbers are extracted without commas or currency symbols. Parentheses in the source indicate negative values; for expense fields, the sign convention is reversed per rule 13, so the extracted number is positive.\n7. The scale is 1,000,000 (millions) as indicated in the statement header.\n8. Other line items in the supplementary tables (e.g., gains/losses on investments, other income/expense components) are not mapped to the requested fields as they are not part of the standard operating cost structure or the specified fields for this extraction.",
